{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,24]],"date-time":"2026-09-24T11:16:57Z","timestamp":1790248617968,"version":"4.1.0"},"reference-count":47,"publisher":"Wiley","issue":"1","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2020,7,18]],"date-time":"2020-07-18T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1595030400000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"}],"funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100000780","name":"European Commission","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["HORIZON2020"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["HORIZON2020"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100000780","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":["rmets.onlinelibrary.wiley.com"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["Geoscience Data Journal"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2021,6]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>The mean radiant temperature (MRT) and the Universal Thermal Climate Index (UTCI) are widely used as human biometeorology parameters to assess the linkages between outdoor environment and human well\u2010being. Historically computed from meteorological station measurements, we here present ERA5\u2010HEAT (Human thErmAl comforT), the first historical dataset of MRT and UTCI as spatially gridded records at the global scale. Derived using climate variables from ERA5, a quality\u2010controlled reanalysis produced by the European Centre for Medium\u2010Range Weather Forecasts (ECMWF) within the Copernicus Climate Change Service (C3S), ERA5\u2010HEAT consists of hourly gridded maps of MRT and UTCI at 0.25\u00b0\u00a0\u00d7\u00a00.25\u00b0 spatial resolution. It currently spans from 1979 to present, and it will be extended in time as updates of ERA5 are made available. ERA5\u2010HEAT provides two streams, a consolidated and an intermediate one, that are released at 2 or 3\u00a0months and 5\u00a0days behind real time, respectively. Data are publicly and freely available for download at the Climate Data Store which has been developed as part of C3S. Being the only existing global historical gridded time series of MRT and UTCI to date, ERA5\u2010HEAT is aimed at a wide range of end users, from scientists to policymakers, with an interest in environment\u2013health applications at any spatial and temporal scale.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1002\/gdj3.102","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2020,7,18]],"date-time":"2020-07-18T06:29:55Z","timestamp":1595053795000},"page":"2-10","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":246,"title":["ERA5\u2010HEAT: A global gridded historical dataset of human thermal comfort indices from climate reanalysis"],"prefix":"10.1002","volume":"8","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-4901-3641","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Claudia","family":"Di Napoli","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"European Centre for Medium\u2010Range Weather Forecasts Reading UK"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-0558-0142","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Christopher","family":"Barnard","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"European Centre for Medium\u2010Range Weather Forecasts Reading UK"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-1722-2497","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Christel","family":"Prudhomme","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"European Centre for Medium\u2010Range Weather Forecasts Reading UK"},{"name":"Centre for Ecology and Hydrology (CEH) Wallingford UK"},{"name":"Department of Geography and Environment University of Loughborough Loughborough UK"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-1472-868X","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Hannah L.","family":"Cloke","sequence